        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=3x\\\\2x-3y&=9\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac97,\\ y=-\\frac{27}{7}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x-3(3x)&=9\\\\-7x&=9\\\\x&=-\\frac97\\\\y&=3\\left(-\\frac97\\right)\\\\y&=-\\frac{27}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $3(-\\frac{9}{7})=-\\frac{27}{7}$ and $2(-\\frac{9}{7})-3(-\\frac{27}{7})=9$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=2y\\\\3x+2y&=6\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac32,\\ y=\\frac34$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3(2y)+2y&=6\\\\8y&=6\\\\y&=\\frac34\\\\x&=2\\left(\\frac34\\right)\\\\x&=\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $2(\\frac{3}{4})=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $3(\\frac{3}{2})+2(\\frac{3}{4})=6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=2x+1\\\\x-3y&=4\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac75,\\ y=-\\frac95$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x-3(2x+1)&=4\\\\x-6x-3&=4\\\\-5x&=7\\\\x&=-\\frac75\\\\y&=2\\left(-\\frac75\\right)+1\\\\y&=-\\frac95\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $2(-\\frac{7}{5})+1=-\\frac{9}{5}$ and $-\\frac{7}{5}-3(-\\frac{9}{5})=4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=1-3y\\\\4x-3y&=12\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{13}{5},\\ y=-\\frac8{15}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4(1-3y)-3y&=12\\\\4-15y&=12\\\\-15y&=8\\\\y&=-\\frac8{15}\\\\x&=1-3\\left(-\\frac8{15}\\right)\\\\x&=\\frac{13}{5}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $1-3(-\\frac{8}{15})=\\frac{13}{5}$ and $4(\\frac{13}{5})-3(-\\frac{8}{15})=12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=1-2x\\\\y&=5x+2\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
